# Call-site ledger of textdistance at faa25f6ff50d0f34dc9655d4d7b0d8daf6f9ff85.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in textdistance.md.
#
# Receivers (B1). Every algorithm class on a public path is a receiver of the
# methods it inherits: a client can build any of them (Base and BaseSimilarity
# too: their __init__ does not raise; the vector_based classes too: the module
# is public, although algorithms/__init__.py does not import it). _NCDBase and
# _BinaryNCDBase are private and never instantiated: only their public
# subclasses are receivers. Method resolution (C = __call__, M = maximum,
# D = distance, S = similarity, ND/NS = normalized_*, Q = quick_answer):
#   Base: C M D S ND NS Q all of Base.
#   BaseSimilarity: C=Base, M=Base, D S Q of BaseSimilarity, ND NS of Base.
#   Base-derived, not BaseSimilarity (D S Q ND NS of Base):
#     Hamming, Levenshtein, DamerauLevenshtein (M=Base); Editex (M=Editex);
#     Length, Bag, Chebyshev, Minkowski, Manhattan, Euclidean, Mahalanobis
#     (M=Base); ArithNCD, RLENCD, BWTRLENCD, SqrtNCD, EntropyNCD (C=_NCDBase,
#     M=_NCDBase); BZ2NCD, LZMANCD, ZLIBNCD (C=_BinaryNCDBase, M=_NCDBase).
#   BaseSimilarity-derived (D S Q of BaseSimilarity, ND NS of Base):
#     JaroWinkler and Jaro (C M of JaroWinkler), SmithWaterman, StrCmp95,
#     MLIPNS, MRA, RatcliffObershelp, Identity, Matrix, Jaccard, Sorensen,
#     Tversky, Overlap, Cosine, MongeElkan (own C and M), Tanimoto (C own,
#     M=Jaccard), Correlation, Kulsinski (own C, M=Base);
#     LCSSeq, LCSStr, Prefix, Postfix (own C, M=Base, S own: Postfix S=Prefix);
#     NeedlemanWunsch (own C M D ND NS minimum), Gotoh (own C M minimum,
#     D ND NS of NeedlemanWunsch).
# Sequences (B2, B4, B5): the compared sequences are client objects; an
# annotation `str` (StrCmp95, Editex, MRA, LCSSeq, LCSStr, RatcliffObershelp)
# fixes str (B4); `Sequence[...]` fixes nothing. The README asks that
# "everything should work not only with strings".
# Callables stored by __init__ (B2): test_func, sim_func, sim_test default to
# Base._ident (a staticmethod); the tests pass a Matrix instance as sim_func of
# NeedlemanWunsch and SmithWaterman (tests/test_edit/test_needleman_wunsch.py:29,
# test_smith_waterman.py:29); SimFunc/TestFunc are aliases of a bare
# Callable, so nothing else is admitted. MongeElkan.algorithm: the default
# DamerauLevenshtein() and the tests' textdistance.jaro_winkler
# (tests/test_token/test_monge_elkan.py:19).

